{
  "example": "`fn[load]` moves to `src/config/load.rs` and its body is also edited. The\nmapped node's hash differs from the recorded one, so `habeas refactor` leaves\nevery record that read it unchanged and reports each one; those records stay\nstale until `habeas author` reassesses them.\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.whole_record`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example gives a concrete case. `fn[load]` moves to `src/config/load.rs` and its body is also edited. Expected behavior: `habeas refactor` leaves every record that read it unchanged, reports each one, and the records stay stale until `habeas author` reassesses them.\n\n`tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_function_edited_while_moving_leaves_its_records_stale]` carries `{test}` references to the example, to `requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`, and to `requirements.refactor.whole_record`.\n\nThe test's setup:\n- `project()` and `author()` write current evidence. `evidence/rules.load.json` reads `src/config.rs#fn[load]` as `inputs[1]`. `evidence/rules.check.json` reads only `fn[check]`, `fn[verify]` and `data.txt`, so `rules.load` is the only record that reads the moved node.\n- `move_load(root, \" parse();\")` moves `load` to `src/config/load.rs` and edits its body, which changes the mapped node's hash.\n- It then runs `refactor` with `--map src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]`.\n\nHow the assertions cover each outcome:\n- **Record left unchanged:** the test reads `evidence/rules.load.json` before the run and asserts the bytes are identical afterward. This covers `whole_record` (the whole record is left unchanged) and `outline_inputs` (the input is not rewritten when the hash differs).\n- **Record reported with the failed check:** the test asserts the report contains `- evidence/rules.load.json: inputs[1]: src/config/load.rs#fn[load] no longer has the recorded hash`. That names the record, the input, and the failed hash check.\n- **Record stays stale:** the test asserts `errors(root)` is non-empty, so validation still flags the record. The assertion is loose because it doesn't name the stale input. The byte-identical file and the specific report line close that gap.\n- **Command succeeds:** the test asserts the command exits successfully.\n\nA refactor that rewrote the input path, rewrote the hash, or omitted the report line would fail these assertions. I found no unresolved gap, and no acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "552027f32d5c09fea2fe5e1c6f72937b3dbf230919da8060b724ff46fe60f71f",
